      "writtenOn": "2018-02-06T13:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes it should\nbtw as expected, the flash subsystem guarantees that the ECC of all FF is FF, so the ECC of blank flash is 10-bit of blank flash.\n\nFor the WP design itself, I\u0027m not sure this would be better than the current scheme (but it\u0027s a bit open since the final security scheme for this firmware is fully designed yet)\nI had the patch to expand the PSTATE code to support write size \u003e 4 bytes to make it compatible with this chip.",
      "parentUuid": "caadc891_90f5190d",
      "revId": "c3ed05793693f80e13fcd15474183801fdcfcf91",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
